Hello All,

Unfortunately in our industry there are several names for the same thing an=
d there can be several things one name can mean.

With Philmac products there are more opportunities for confusion.

We recently had a case where a customer bought some 3G IPS-OD fittings for =
use on steel pipe claiming we told him he could.  Of course they blew off t=
he pipe when they got up to pressure because the collets/grip rings cannot =
grip steel pipe.

It would be possible to interpret a question:  "Will your Philmac 3G compre=
ssion fitting work on steel pipe?" as "Will your Philmac 3G compression fit=
ting work on steel pipe sizes?".  The term "steel pipe sizes" is of course =
another way of referring to IPS.  In this case the customer really wanted a=
 fitting for use on steel pipe which the 3G fittings will not work on (the =
UTC will work on steel pipe however)."

The 3G fittings only work on PE pipe except they can be fitted out with ada=
pters in some cases/sizes that allow them to be used on copper tubing or PV=
C (in IPS).  In the case of copper tubing this would be for =BE" and 1" onl=
y.

When in doubt, call me.

John

--_000_004c01cc31ebec391020c4ab3060harcofittingscom_
